If each agent $v\in\Vnet$ uses adaptive learning rates equal to $\eta_t(v)=0$ for $t\leq n+1$, $\eta_t(v) = \sqrt{\fracc{\log (K)}{\sum_{s=1}^t X_s(v)}}$ with $X_t(v)= 

n  + \sum_{i\in\Vfeed} \frac{ p_t(i,v) }{b_t(i,v)}
$ for $t>n+1$, the average network regret of \ouralg{} playing with an \oni{} can be bounded as
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:main}
    \frac{R_T}{Q}
\overset{\widetilde \cO}{=}
      \sqrt{ \log (K) \left(n+1+\frac{\alpha\left(N^n \boxtimes F\right)}{Q} \right) T}\;.
\end{equation}
